    "text": "A finite group G is said to be semi-abelian if it has a sequence of subgroups\n1 = G0 ⩽ G1 ⩽ · · · ⩽ Gn = G such that for every i the subgroup Gi+1 is isomorphic\nto a quotient of a semidirect product Ai ⋊ Gi for some abelian group Ai .\n    Conjecture: Semi-abelian finite groups are monomial.                     M. Kida",
